"""
Patient Simulator — a text-based diagnostic training tool.

Doctors pick a ward, meet a FRESHLY GENERATED patient (a random disease
from that ward combined with a randomly assembled profile — name, age,
gender, symptoms, history, medications, vitals), then interrogate the
"patient" in a Q&A loop. Answers are generated by Google's Gemini API
(free tier, generous daily request limits — no per-token billing needed
for practice use) when an API key is available, and fall back to a
lightweight rule-based responder otherwise, so the script always runs
offline.

IMPORTANT DESIGN POINT: patient profiles are NOT a hardcoded list to pick
from. Each disease defines *pools* of plausible symptoms, history factors,
medications, an age range, and vital-sign ranges. Every new session:
  1. Picks a random disease from the chosen ward.
  2. Uses Faker (if installed) to generate a brand-new name/age/gender.
  3. Randomly samples a handful of symptoms/history items/medications from
     that disease's pools.
  4. Randomizes vitals within clinically plausible ranges for that disease.
This means the pool of *possible* patients is effectively unlimited, even
though the underlying medical knowledge (which symptoms/history fit which
disease) stays curated and clinically sensible.

The core logic lives in `PatientSimulator`, a plain Python class with no
I/O side effects of its own — this is deliberate so the exact same class
can be dropped behind a FastAPI/Flask endpoint later (see the commented
`api.py` sketch at the bottom of this file) without touching the CLI code.

Run it directly for a terminal session:
    python patient_simulator.py

Optional:
    pip install faker                 -> unique random names every run
    pip install google-genai          -> LLM-generated answers via Gemini
    export GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...      -> enables the LLM path
Without either, the script still runs fully offline with built-in fallbacks.

Getting a free Gemini API key: visit https://aistudio.google.com/apikey,
sign in with a Google account, and click "Create API key" — no credit
card required for the free tier. Free-tier daily limits are generous
(hundreds of requests/day on Flash models), which is effectively
unlimited for practicing consultations.
"""

